claim.claim-text:
1. A method for managing data in a computing environment using one or more processors to execute instructions that are configured to cause actions, comprising:
obtaining one or more context records from a repository, wherein each context record includes supplemental information associated with one or more events;
collecting one or more severity scores for the one or more events based on one or more prompts and the one or more context records, wherein the one or more context records are included in the one or more prompts;
obtaining a criteria to invalidate a portion of the one or more context records, wherein the criteria includes one or more of an age of a context record, a source reliability, a conflict with one or more other context records, or a usage frequency;
modifying the one or more prompts and the repository based on removal of the invalidated portion of the one or more context records;
collecting one or more other severity scores for one or more other events based on the one or more modified prompts, wherein the one or more other severity scores are used to evaluate the one or more events for a report; and
obtaining a user interface that includes one or more display panels for content that includes the report and other information associated with the one or more other events, wherein the content is dynamically transformed and arranged for display to a user based on user interaction telemetry, user feedback and telemetry metrics.

11. A network computer for managing data in a computing environment, comprising:
a memory that stores at least instructions; and
